---
import Main from "@/layouts/Main.astro";
import PageHeader from "@/components/PageHeader.astro";
import StepCard from "@/components/StepCard.astro";
import FeatureCard from "@/components/FeatureCard.astro";
---

<Main
  title="Buy: Sovereign Canadian compute and compute credits"
  description="Purchase Canadian AI compute capacity and compute credits (prepaid usage credits) through conventional commercial contracts. Managed by DAI Compute."
  activePath="/buy"
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Buy"
    title="Purchase Canadian compute and compute credits."
    lede="Start with the workload, controls, and service outcome you need. Procure managed capacity, reserved capacity, or a dedicated deployment through conventional commercial contracts. Compute credits are prepaid usage credits, not speculative tokens."
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
    <p class="field-label" style="color: var(--color-yellow);">How it works</p>
    <h2 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-display text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-snow">
      Workload first. Capacity second. Token speculation never.
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <StepCard index="01" title="Map the workload">
        Describe performance, data residency, control, and assurance needs. We
        help determine whether managed, reserved, or dedicated capacity fits.
      </StepCard>
      <StepCard index="02" title="Contract conventionally">
        Approved services are intended to be procured through ordinary commercial
        contracts and payment methods: invoice, bank transfer, or other supported
        methods once the contracting entity is live.
      </StepCard>
      <StepCard index="03" title="Use compute credits">
        Compute credits are prepaid usage credits for Canadian capacity. They are
        not an investment product and do not require a blockchain wallet.
      </StepCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-hairline bg-ink-2/30">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
      <p class="field-label" style="color: var(--color-yellow);">What you can buy</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-display text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-snow">
        Capacity shaped to the operating requirement.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <FeatureCard kicker="Managed" title="Network capacity" accent="yellow">
          Access Canadian-managed compute capacity coordinated by DAI Compute,
          with service boundaries agreed in contract.
        </FeatureCard>
        <FeatureCard kicker="Reserved" title="Dedicated capacity" accent="yellow">
          Reserve capacity for regulated or high-assurance workloads where
          isolation and policy controls matter.
        </FeatureCard>
        <FeatureCard kicker="Credits" title="Compute credits" accent="yellow">
          Prepaid usage credits for AI workloads. Traditional commercial
          accounting, not crypto speculation.
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate">
      <p class="field-label" style="color: var(--color-yellow);">Sovereignty posture</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-snow sm:text-3xl">
        Canadian residency is one part of the assessment.
      </h2>
      <p>
        Buyers should assess control, access, key custody, data flows, and
        jurisdiction, not postal code alone. Where a provider subject to U.S. law
        has possession, custody, or control of data, U.S. legal process may be
        relevant even when data is stored in Canada. See
        <a href="/sovereignty" class="accent-link">Sovereignty</a> for the
        problem framing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Capacity procurement does not require token use. Optional
        network-participation mechanisms are described under
        <a href="/technology" class="accent-link">Technology</a> and are not
        available for purchase today.
      </p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary mt-6 inline-flex items-center px-7 py-3.5 text-sm">
        Request a workload assessment
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Main>
